mab776 (2026-10-17): GGML_BATCH_INVARIANT=C (opt-in; unset / 0 = the stock kernels) - a decode-sized matmul or flash
attention (<= 8 rows) computes every row with the arithmetic of a 1-row call, so a DSpark verify pass's rows match a
one-token decode bit for bit whatever the depth / number of drafts:
  - float weights (F32 / F16 / BF16: the HC mixes, compressors, indexer, router) always on the vector kernel (mmvf) - its
    per-column reduction does not depend on the column count (stock: 2..8 rows can go to the mmf tensor-core tiles);
  - quantized weights (MMVQ) launch the 1-column warp count for 2..8 columns (stock: 4 warps up to 4 columns, 2 above, and
    a small-K variant at 1 column only);
  - no fused 1-row epilogues (ggml_cuda_should_fuse_mul_mat_vec_f/q return false for MUL_MAT): 2..8 rows never fuse;
  - flash attention splits each output tile's KV range into C blocks (stream-K: C blocks per tile; else C parallel blocks)
    instead of an occupancy-sized split that changes with the number of query tiles; prompt batches keep the stock split.
Apply after the other tools/v41/ggml patches: patch -p1 -d third_party/llama.cpp < tools/v41/ggml/mab776-batch-invariant.patch

